<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite — Code-to-model traceability: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Positives: every math-KG locus now starts at the declaration or `def` it cites and lies within its file (checked programmatically; `verify_integrity.py --loop-yaml` passes) (closes R6); docs/bioelectricity/ levin_youtube_kg.json is regenerated for the 8-law suite with schema 3.0.0, 17 concepts, a criteria rubric and the v2 referee block (closes R5); verify_integrity.py implements check_math_kg_loop_yaml and a conclusion-aware Lean classifier, LOOPS_MATH_DIR is used, `loan_body` is gone (closes R10's code part); the suite's own classifier applies the same bound-name-in-conclusion rule (L142-L153); C4 is claimed only by Laws 4 and 8 and C2 is withdrawn from Laws 5 and 7, consistently in the script, YAML, docs and KG (closes R8); the O1/O2 and T1-T4 counts agree across the four artefacts; both Lean modules compile with 0 sorry. Deductions: the written record disagrees with the code in at least seven places - criteria doc L62 (+0.7618), L64 / YAML L112 / KG L583 (0.0020 -> 0.9036), script L12 (101 values), L13-L14 and L182-L183 (Hill fit + RMS), L25 (alpha 0.95), L33-L35 (plasticity, extinction), L461-L469 (different ODE and results) (-10); the KG payload's `verified_measurements` is the referee's Pass 3 sidecar describing superseded code, and no generator script for the payload exists (-5); C3 for Laws 4, 5, 7 rests on the soft 'in the primary source' clause with a single implemented_by each (-3); MathOfBiology.lean section 17 is a maintained textual duplicate rather than an import (-2); the Lean classifiers are regex-based and would still accept a conclusion that mentions a bound name trivially (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md L33–L33: C4 rule still cites 'alpha_bias -> 0.95' as the regime-crossing example; the code sweeps to 0.90 (L390) and the table (L62) reports a slope value the code does not produce <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md#L33-L33>",
        "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L583–L583: Law 6 role text '0.0020 pre-training -> 0.9036 post-training' in the regenerated payload; the payload's own domain_summary (L1150) records intervened_metric_pre 0.0015 and metric 1.0 for the same law - the file contradicts itself <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L583-L583>",
        "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L672–L686: verified_measurements = this referee's Pass 3 sidecar (meas_id ...-v3-...-m1 .. m22) copied verbatim, including 'Law 1 is the v2 one-point formula with an unused solver' and 'slope -0.1556'; stale with respect to the Pass 3.1 code the payload otherwise describes. No script generates the payload <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L672-L686>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L757–L757: Law 4 criteria_passed C1, C2, C3, C4 with implemented_by = this script only (L758): C3 ('>= 2 implementations or cross-substrate validation in the primary source') rests on the soft clause; same for Laws 5 and 7 (single implemented_by) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L757-L757>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-7> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Verified by running: Law 1's BVP reach is the metric and the asserted quantity, with an independent continuum closed form 31.51 vs 32.01 (+8 of the -8 restored, less -2 for the unimplemented Hill fit/RMS the docstring promises); Law 4 keeps r_exit fixed and breaks detailed balance through a non-doubly- stochastic K_trap - re-derived here: K_trap column sums range 0.15..1.9, so p ∝ 1/r genuinely fails and the slope moves -1.0000 / -0.5598 / +0.1866 against the untouched rates (+8 of -10 restored; -2 because the criteria doc reports +0.7618, a value no run produces); Law 3's edge coefficients are Pade(1,1) and the error falls 7.4e-3 -> 2.5e-5 over N = 15..240 with ratio ~4.1 per doubling, a genuine O(h^2) convergence to exp(dV/V_T) (+4 of -5; the G_gj spread remains linear algebra); Law 6 replaces the tanh unit with a 3-node ODE whose CS-only response 0.0015 -> 1.0 depends on a slow memory node that survives a washout (+3 of -6; -3 kept because the docstring describes a different circuit with different results and the header promises plasticity and extinction that do not exist). Unchanged deductions: Law 2's I_ion is an invented cubic and the wound is a hard clamp (-4); Law 8's k >= 17 threshold applies the square-lattice fraction to non-square k and pi_D is the builder's construction (-4); Law 5 is a 4-row truth table (-3); Law 2's and Law 7's Lean theorems state much less than their names claim (-2); panel A overlays Law 1 on a scaled G_gj axis shared with the cell index (-1); Law 1's `hill_curve` is dead output (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md L62–L62: Law 4 row: 'unconfounded C4 breakdown at alpha = 0.90 -> +0.7618'. The code produces +0.1866 (summary JSON c4_unconfounded_slope_alpha090, --self-test, KG payload L1101); no parameterisation reachable from the CLI was found that yields 0.7618 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md#L62-L62>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L12–L14: Header: 'sweeps G_gj across 101 values, and fits the phenomenological Hill curve to the PDE curve (reporting the exact RMS residual)'. Code: 51 values (L203), no fit, no residual <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L12-L14>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L182–L183: Docstring: 'evaluate the phenomenological Hill approximation with fitted half-saturation G_eff and report the RMS residual between the PDE and Hill curves'. No fit and no residual exist in the function; `hill_curve` (L211) uses the unfitted G_half and is returned at L224 then dropped at L860. Referee: RMS(Hill - PDE) = 55.2 cells over the grid; best-fit G_eff = 2.26 (RMS 3.05) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L182-L183>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L231–L277: Law 2 unchanged since Pass 3: 20-cell ODE, cubic I_ion with roots -60 / -38 / -10 mV, hard clamp of cells 0-4; gated tail -60.003 mV vs ohmic -10.0 mV (reproduced). Genuine two-regime dynamics on an invented current <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L231-L277>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L25–L25: Header: 'alpha_bias in [0, 0.95]'; the sweep stops at 0.90 (L390) and the docstring at L344 says [0, 0.90] <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L25-L25>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L315–L317: Law 3 G_gj sweep: G_gj multiplies every entry of Q (L301-L302), so the nullspace ratio is invariant by linear algebra; spread 1e-12 is guaranteed, not a result about electrodiffusion <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L315-L317>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L31–L35: Header: 'integrates a 3-node transcription-factor ODE network with slow associative weight plasticity (w_CS_M), measuring conditioning acquisition and extinction'. No weight variable, no plasticity rule and no extinction phase exist in the code (L506-L527): the coupling 0.90 is a constant and memory is a state variable <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L31-L35>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L413–L418: Law 5: the same 4-row x 3-gate truth table as v2 and Pass 3 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L413-L418>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L461–L469: Law 6 docstring: dx_M = -0.2 x_M + sigma(8 (x_CS x_US - 0.35)), dx_US = -x_US + sigma(8 (I_US + 1.8 x_M x_CS - 0.50)), pre 0.023, post 0.909. Code (L508-L513): -0.02 x_M + 0.25 sigma(12 (... - 0.50)), sigma(12 (I_US + 0.90 x_M x_CS - 0.55)), pre 0.0015, post 1.0. The documented model is not the implemented model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L461-L469>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L550–L560: Law 8 unchanged: thresholds k = 4, 16, 17 from applying 1 - 1/sqrt(k) to all k = 1..36; k = 17 is not realised by any m x m cluster (first exact square with strict dominance is k = 25); pi_D = b / sqrt(k) is the builder's construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L550-L560>",
        "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L607–L612: Panel A: Law 1 reach curve plotted on a twin y-axis against g_scaled = g_grid * 9.5 so that G_gj in [0, 2] spans the 0..19 cell-index axis (L608); the x-axis label reads 'Cell Index i (0..19) / Scaled G_gj'. Law 1 is now plotted (remediates R1's 'no panel') but on a borrowed, rescaled abscissa with no tick labels of its own <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L607-L612>",
        "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L235–L250: Law 7 theorem: integer telescoping and 0 < (e - f) - (a - b) ↔ a - b < e - f for all Int; no reference to a TPM, determinism or degeneracy; unchanged <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L235-L250>",
        "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L71–L97: Law 2 theorem named 'wound_isolation' proves symmetry/monotonicity of (1 + b_i)(1 + b_j) and antisymmetry of g (v_j - v_i). No bistability, isolation or ODE property is stated; unchanged since Pass 3 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L71-L97>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-9> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite — Morphometric validation: 44/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "What exists now: Law 3's convergence is a real numerical validation against an independent closed form (error 2.5e-5 at N = 240, O(h^2)); Law 1's BVP is checked against its continuum limit (31.51 vs 32.01, 1.6 %); Law 4's slope change is a measured property of the generator, not a regressor swap; Law 6's basin fraction (0 -> 1) and conditioning response (0.0015 -> 1.0) are non-identity outcomes; Delta E = -eta N^2 is labelled an identity; Law 7's Delta CP values are pinned to a hash-verified committed artefact; the Law 2 isolation ratio e^10 and the Law 8 bond fractions were re-derived. Deductions: no measurement is compared with a value measured on an organism, an experiment or a figure in any cited paper - Chvykov 2021's measured enrichment, Pigozzi 2025's conditioning success, Cervera 2020's voltage levels and Pietak 2016's BETSE gradients all exist and none is used (-30); the Law 3 G_gj spread and the Law 8 threshold comparisons remain same-expression checks (-8); the documented outcome values do not match the computed ones (+0.7618 vs +0.1866; 0.0020 -> 0.9036 vs 0.0015 -> 1.0; 0.023 -> 0.909 in the docstring), so the written record of the validation is wrong in three places (-8); the builder still ships no measurements sidecar - the KG payload's `verified_measurements` is a copy of the referee's Pass 3 sidecar describing the superseded code (-6); the CE2 reference is repository-internal (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L672–L686: verified_measurements m1: 'Referee count - laws whose Python evaluation is ... not fixed by construction', value 3, method text 'Law 1 is the v2 one-point formula with an unused solver' - the referee's Pass 3 sidecar copied verbatim into the regenerated 8-law payload, describing code that no longer exists <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L672-L686>",
        "morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml L112–L112: Law 6 role: 'CS-only US activation 0.0020 pre-training -> 0.9036 post-training'. Code output: 0.0015 -> 1.0 (summary JSON grn_3node_us_response_cs_only_pre/post; --self-test). Same wrong values in docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md L64 and docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L583 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/1969a7ea/morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml#L112-L112>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-catalog-verification-cited-video-ids-resolving-in-the-374-video-catalog-with-sha-256-pin>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-cli-expressivity-model-flags-that-complete-a-self-test-run-with-a-non-default-value>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-bvp-spatial-reach-at-g-gj-1-0-n-100-g-half-0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-hill-formula-1-n-1-g-g-g-half-at-g-gj-1-0-and-its-residual-against-the-bvp>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-bell-conductance-isolation-ratio-g-60-60-g-10-10-at-v-th-35-v-0-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-healthy-tail-v-mem-bell-gated-vs-ohmic-control-t-80>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-absolute-error-of-c-post-c-ant-vs-exp-dv-v-t-across-n-ap-15-30-60-120-240>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-central-difference-c-post-c-ant-at-dv-40-mv-n-ap-120-g-gj-1-0>,
